ping and the recorder that the assertion reads.\n- Keep every register named by an `==` case term on an operand field, such as `rs1==6`. The value read from it must equal the ILA's value at the start. This includes x0 when `rs1==0`, because the ILA reads its x0 state, which is only zero under its assumption.\n- Every other register is irrelevant to the comparison, so it becomes `havoc`. This also covers x_k.frame, where the source register is unconstrained.\n\n**Units**\n- **Register sub-properties (`xk.*`):** cut all three units. The checked instruction comes from the wrapper's constrained `near_mem$imem_instr`, not from the instruction cache. The data cache serves only loads and stores. The CSR file and cache outputs only affect traps, stalls and reset, which should either make the run vacuous or leave x_k unwritten. The frame case holds either way. For the write cases, I assume a trapped instruction never reaches the instruction end; if that is wrong, refinement has to restore the units, provided it applies to units at all.\n- **Other states (`mem`, `pc`, branches, stores):** keep the instruction cache, because the compared pc is `near_mem$imem_pc`. Keep the CSR file, because traps and their target address affect pc. The data cache is cut only when the compared states are limited to pc, load_en, store_en and x0. Otherwise, such as for store address or data states, it is kept.\n\n**Operators**\n- Keep all of them. A `uf` adds no state-bit savings, because its operands' cones (register file reads, bypass registers) stay in the model anyway. It only adds risk of spurious counterexamples. RV32I operators are cheap enough to keep.\n\n```python\ndef gpr_state_num(s):\n    if len(s) >= 2 and s[0] == \"x\" and s[1:].isdigit():\n        return int(s[1:])\n    return -1\n\n\ndef choose(sub, design):\n    states = sub.get(\"states\", []) or []\n    terms = sub.get(\"case_terms\", []) or []\n    op_fields = design.get(\"operand_fields\", []) or []\n\n    gpr_states = set()\n    other_states = []\n    for s in states:\n        n = gpr_state_num(s)\n        if n >= 1:\n            gpr_states.add(n)\n        elif n == 0:\n            other_states.append(s)\n        else:\n            other_states.append(s)\n\n    # registers that must stay exact\n    needed = set(gpr_states)\n    for t in terms:\n        f = t.get(\"field\")\n        if t.get(\"op\") == \"==\" and (f in op_fields or f in [\"rs1\", \"rs2\"]):\n            v = t.get(\"value\")\n            if isinstance(v, int) and 0 <= v <= 31:\n                needed.add(v)\n    if \"x0\" in states:\n        needed.add(0)\n\n    gpr_only = len(gpr_states) > 0 and len(other_states) == 0\n    simple_states = set([\"pc\", \"x0\", \"load_en\", \"store_en\"])\n    only_simple = all(s in simple_states for s in other_states)\n\n    out = {}\n    for c in design.get(\"choices\", []):\n        cid = c[\"id\"]\n        kind = c.get(\"kind\")\n        levels = c.get(\"levels\", [])\n        lvl = levels[0] if len(levels) > 0 else \"keep\"\n        if kind == \"gpr\":\n            r = c.get(\"register\")\n            if r in needed:\n                lvl = \"keep\"\n            elif \"havoc\" in levels:\n                lvl = \"havoc\"\n            elif \"word\" in levels:\n                lvl = \"word\"\n            else:\n                lvl = \"keep\"\n        elif kind == \"unit\":\n            inst = str(c.get(\"instance\", \"\"))\n            parts = inst.replace(\".\", \" \").split()\n            last = parts[-1] if len(parts) > 0 else \"\"\n            if gpr_only:\n                lvl = \"cut\" if \"cut\" in levels else \"keep\"\n            else:\n                if last == \"dcache\" and only_simple and \"cut\" in levels:\n                    lvl = \"cut\"\n                else:\n                    lvl = \"keep\"\n        elif kind == \"operator\":\n            lvl = \"keep\" if \"keep\" in levels else lvl\n        else:\n            lvl = \"keep\" if \"keep\" in levels else lvl\n        if lvl not in levels and len(levels) > 0:\n            lvl = levels[0]\n        out[cid] = lvl\n    return out\n```","ttft_ms":63203,"type":"result","duration_ms":76746,"uuid":"847b9753-6c93-4842-9290-7252615409f5","ttft_stream_ms":3407,"time_to_request_ms":40,"first_content_frame_ms":3407,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
